  "headline": "Indonesian Parliament Sets December Deadline For Vice President Vote",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Sets December Date For Vice President Vote",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian parliament scheduled the vice president election for December 9, following a request to replace outgoing official Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The People's Consultative Assembly scheduled the vice presidential election for December 9, 2026.",
    "President Prabowo must submit two potential vice presidential candidates to the assembly by November 25.",
    "Prominent names within the Gerindra party are being discussed as potential successors for the vacant position."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian political landscape is currently centered on the process of selecting a new vice president following the vacancy left by Gibran Rakabuming Raka. The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has formally received a submission from President Prabowo regarding the replacement process and has adjusted its plenary session schedule to accommodate the election on December 9, 2026. Official procedures dictate that the President must finalize and submit two candidate names by November 25. Political discourse is currently focused on potential nominees, with various parties signaling their positions on candidates emerging from the Gerindra party. Among those mentioned in speculative discussions are senior party figures such as Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, Ahmad Muzani, and Sugiono. While the selection process moves through institutional channels, political organizations have expressed their stances on the prospect of a candidate originating from the ruling party.",
